# Recording corrections

A correction that the owner gives in conversation lands in the same change as the work, in the file where it belongs:

- A working rule: one `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, one concern per file, with a BAD and a GOOD example.
- The meaning of the product: `docs/design.ja.md` (through a `design` Issue when it changes the spec).
- A rejected alternative: `docs/design-decisions.md`.
- A decision and its measured reason: an ADR in `docs/adr/`.
- A step-by-step procedure: the matching skill under `.agents/skills/` (and its copy under `.claude/skills/`).

A lesson first noticed at the retrospective after a merge is written the same way, without waiting for an ask (`.cursor/rules/workflow.mdc`).

The agent's own memory is not one of these places. A note there is read by one tool on one machine, and by no reviewer. A correction that should hold next time is a file in this repository.

```text
# BAD
Owner: 署名の比較は定数時間でやる約束では？
Agent: rewrites the comparison, and saves "constant-time compare" to its memory directory

# GOOD
Owner: 署名の比較は定数時間でやる約束では？
Agent: rewrites the comparison, and adds the case to .cursor/rules/security.mdc in the same PR
```

A rule only says to follow the design. It does not copy the design's type lists, section text, or figures.
